The Ashen Pact is a set of six gods: [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/War|War]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Esoterica|Esoterica]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Regent|Regent]]. Their likenesses stand on the six wrought-iron doors of the heptagonal chamber deep in the fane beneath the [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/Gas-n-Go|Gas-n-Go]], where [[Org/Roundhat Gang/People/Tywelwyn Leatherhide|Tywelwyn]] kept them.

The [[Geography/Calaria/Hallia/Widdershins/An Iron Gauntlet in a Glass Glove|Heart]] in that chamber, made by Tywelwyn, calls them its own gods, inherited from its maker. It says they come from a Godhome and want to visit their blessings on [[Færrin]]: eternal fire, torment and a clean slate. Tywelwyn's death has held off their coming for a while, and they are not here now. The [[Org/Embercall Industries/index|Embercall]] is for Pyre, and Pyre is the one who told Tywelwyn how to make a Heart.

Behind each door lies a room of the fane: Pyre's bedroom, Herald's armory, Giant's radar dish plant and pilgrimage rooms, War's office, Esoterica's haberdasher, and Regent's orrery.

Under the harmony that the true kin of [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] carry in their sleep run the words *ashen pact*. [[People/Anzu|Anzu]] heard them when he reached into the mind of one of the sleepers, and saw all six of the gods standing at the horizon of a grassy plain, looking down on it as builders look on a model while it burned, with the strange-angled city of his first [[Phenomena/Harmony/Voidsong|Voidsong]] dream in the distance.

[[Org/Iconoclasm/People/Anaïs Marchal|Anaïs Marchal]] knows three of the six names, [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Pyre|Pyre]], [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Herald|Herald]] and [[Divinity/Ashen Pact/Giant|Giant]], from talk of the narrative siblings, but has never heard the others spoken of as destroyers.
